{"98131": "<!--\n  HOW THIS PAGE WORKS\n\n  The div below is the whole tool. It has no code of its own. Every\n  interactive tool on the site is the same runner (snippet 137, the Alpha\n  Tool Runner) pointed at a different data file. This page points at\n  jayms-tool-data/divine-council-alpha.json, 33 entries.\n\n  Two places to change things, and only two:\n\n  THE DATA FILE  the entries, the filter rows and their options,\n                 the detail boxes, what search is allowed to read.\n  THIS DIV       how all of that is presented.\n\n  Neither one is a snippet. If something needs changing it is one of these\n  two, never the runner. Change the runner and you change all six tools at\n  once.\n\n  WHAT EACH ATTRIBUTE HERE IS DOING\n\n  data-layout=\"rail\"              grid, list or rail\n  data-filters=\"category:open, group:open, witness:open\"\n                                  which filter rows appear, in this order, and how.\n                                    field:open prints the chips, field:fold puts them behind a\n                                    dropdown, field:off hides the row.\n  data-search=\"text\"              text searches inside the fields the data file names.\n                                    \"name\" matches the start of a name and forgives a letter\n                                    or two of spelling. \"both\" accepts either. \"off\" hides the box.\n  data-main=\"plain\"               which field fills a row's information area\n  data-tags=\"none\"                which filter rows print as tags on a row. \"none\" for no tags\n  data-progress=\"on\"              the done checkbox\n  data-suggest=\"on\"               the suggest an entry box at the foot\n\n  WHICH ROW DRIVES THE LEFT RAIL\n\n  Not this page, the data file. Here it is the \"group\" row, headed \"All\n  threads\", because it is the first row that is not the verdict row:\n  Council and assembly, Cosmic geography, Rebellion 1 · Eden, Rebellion 2\n  · the Watchers, Two powers and elohim, The reversal.\n\n  AVAILABLE BUT NOT USED HERE\n\n  data-columns        grid width: auto, 2, 3 or 4\n  data-per-page       rows per page, the rail included\n  data-row            columns puts a row's label beside the text, stack above it\n  data-filters-hide   drop a filter row entirely\n  data-default-group  the filter a cold visit lands on\n  data-label          which field sets a row's left column\n  data-sub            which field sets a row's second line\n  data-badge          the verdict badge on a row\n\n  Fuller notes live in JAYMS-bible-tools-infrastructure.md.\n-->\n<div class=\"wrap jayms-tool-alpha\" id=\"app\" data-layout=\"rail\" data-filters=\"category:open, group:open, witness:open\" data-search=\"text\" data-main=\"plain\" data-tags=\"none\" data-progress=\"on\" data-suggest=\"on\"></div>", "98132": "<!--\n  HOW THIS PAGE WORKS\n\n  The div below is the whole tool. It has no code of its own. Every\n  interactive tool on the site is the same runner (snippet 137, the Alpha\n  Tool Runner) pointed at a different data file. This page points at\n  jayms-tool-data/gods-of-the-bible-alpha.json, 107 entries.\n\n  Two places to change things, and only two:\n\n  THE DATA FILE  the entries, the filter rows and their options,\n                 the detail boxes, what search is allowed to read.\n  THIS DIV       how all of that is presented.\n\n  Neither one is a snippet. If something needs changing it is one of these\n  two, never the runner. Change the runner and you change all six tools at\n  once.\n\n  WHAT EACH ATTRIBUTE HERE IS DOING\n\n  data-layout=\"rail\"              grid, list or rail\n  data-filters=\"category:open, group:open, testament:fold\"\n                                  which filter rows appear, in this order, and how.\n                                    field:open prints the chips, field:fold puts them behind a\n                                    dropdown, field:off hides the row.\n  data-search=\"text\"              t